# El-Imtiyaz Parent Portal — environment template
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in the values from the canonical credential
# sheet: docs/operations/credentials.md in the hub repository
# (AgentGithubUplaod). The Supabase URL and public API key below are the REAL
# production values (both are public client-side identifiers — they are
# designed to ship inside the browser bundle and are protected by RLS,
# not by secrecy). Firebase web config is likewise public.
#
# T-107 / MIG-KEYS-201 (2026-09-01, ADR-009): NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
# now carries the NEW-FORMAT publishable key (sb_publishable_…). The legacy
# anon JWT was project-scoped to the OLD project and was REMOVED in T-516 —
# a new legacy anon JWT for the current project exists in the Supabase
# dashboard (Settings → API Keys) and remains dual-accepted per ADR-009.
# NEVER put the service_role key, the server secret key or any other
# server-side credential in this file — it is compiled into the client bundle.

# ── Supabase (shared backend — same project as desktop + Android) ──────────
# T-096 (2026-08-31): the URL and API key below are the REAL production
# values, committed because they are public client identifiers (they ship in
# the browser bundle regardless). The portal ALSO falls back to these values
# at runtime via src/lib/public-config.ts — a fresh clone works without this
# file. Copy to .env.local ONLY to override (e.g. point at a different
# project for testing).
# T-107 / MIG-KEYS-201: the key below is the new-format PUBLISHABLE key.
# T-516 / CONFIG-500 (2026-10-13): cutover to the current live project
# `vebfehrpzajhstyhinnw` (live since the 2026-09-17 switch). The previous
# values pointed at the abandoned `hkvkefubghbbotgnteir` project.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://vebfehrpzajhstyhinnw.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_IPUtQMYQzr1wNnfGTcl5MA_wuz3RUdg

# ── Firebase web (FCM push notifications) ──────────────────────────────────
# T-519 / CONFIG-501 (2026-10-13): cutover to the owner's NEW Firebase project
# `elimtiyaz-production` (a real WEB app id now exists). The previous values
# pointed at the OLD `elimtiyaz-android` project, which had no web app
# registered. All values below are public web config.
# T-520 / CONFIG-502 (2026-10-13): the owner generated the Web Push
# certificate in the new Firebase console (Project settings → Cloud Messaging
# → Web Push Certificates) and supplied its PUBLIC key — the last open value.
# Web push is now ENABLED out of the box (isFcmConfigured = true on a fresh
# clone); the [env] Firebase warning is silenced. No Vercel env var is
# needed: the committed default in src/lib/public-config.ts rules the
# production bundle (the T-516/T-519 pattern). Copy to .env.local ONLY to
# override — e.g. set NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_VAPID_KEY= (empty) to deliberately
# disable push on a test build. The project's measurementId (G-G3YGN1WZF3,
# Analytics-only) is recorded in the hub credentials sheet §9.6; the portal
# imports no firebase/analytics, so it has no env slot here.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSyByguKxez7hNjkGcdLnbTCHLI5nJzEFqvY
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=elimtiyaz-production.firebaseapp.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=elimtiyaz-production
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=elimtiyaz-production.firebasestorage.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=944201689219
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:944201689219:web:b5fbe39a56e09c7629d3b6
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_VAPID_KEY=BK08KLwqnYj-d6jPE3laBEHvBoR89iqE7i3u-Jssn1NhaiGnniNnUI3Ty_k4Sgqd0QEfWixfNSV4PoynuwWoEo8

# ── Portal behaviour ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_NAME="El-Imtiyaz Portal"
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEFAULT_LOCALE=fr
